21. Taking Thread Dump

First:

jps -l

Then:

jstack 12345

Save it:

jstack 2969 > threaddump.txt

Modern JVM:

jcmd 12345 Thread.print

You can take multiple thread dumps:

jstack PID > thread1.txt

sleep 10

jstack PID > thread2.txt

sleep 10

jstack PID > thread3.txt

This is much more useful than taking only one.

Why?

Because you can compare:

T1
T2
T3

and see which threads remain stuck.



29. Enable GC Logging — Java 17+

For Java 17:

-Xlog:gc*:file=gc.log:time,uptime,level,tags

Example:

java \
-Xms2g \
-Xmx4g \
-Xlog:gc*:file=/var/log/app/gc.log:time,uptime,level,tags \
-jar application.jar

X → “eXtension” flag: a non‑standard but widely supported JVM option prefix.

m → memory (heap size).

s → start / initial heap size.

x → maximum heap size.

So:

-Xms2g = set the initial (and minimum) Java heap to 2 GB.

-Xmx4g = set the maximum Java heap to 4 GB.

